# Virtual environment
# `.venv*/` is a glob, not a literal: a worktree can't share the main checkout's
# editable install, so per-worktree venvs get suffixed names (.venv-wt, .venv-ci,
# .venv-audit) that a bare `.venv/` left as thousands of untracked files.
# Deliberately unanchored — those venvs live under .claude/worktrees/*/, so a
# leading slash would miss the exact case this covers.
# `venv/` stays a literal on purpose: the three tests/architecture/ sweeps skip
# the names ".venv"/"venv" and any dot-prefixed dir, so globbing the undotted form
# would let a `venv311/` be walked by them while being invisible to git status —
# a diagnosable mess turned into an undiagnosable one.
.venv*/
venv/
ENV/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
